c=A.u3(A.b(["Step 1: Visit official PM-KISAN portal (pmkisan.gov.in) or visit nearest Common Service Center (CSC).",'Step 2: Click on "Farmers Corner" -> "New Farmer Registration".',"Step 3: Enter Rural/Urban registration, Aadhaar number, Mobile number, and State.","Step 4: Fill land ownership details, survey numbers, and submit for District Nodal Officer verification."],f),d,"Income Support","Central Sector scheme with 100% funding from Government of India to provide income support to all landholding farmer families across the country to enable them to take care of expenses related to agriculture and domestic needs.",e,"scheme_pm_kisan",j,"Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman Nidhi (PM-KISAN)","Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare, Govt of India","https://pmkisan.gov.in",c,"Direct financial assistance of \u20b96,000 per year in three equal installments of \u20b92,000.")
e=A.b(["All farmers including sharecroppers and tenant farmers growing notified crops in notified areas.","Both loanee and non-loanee farmers are eligible."],f)
d=A.b(["Very low premium payable by farmer: Max 2% for Kharif food/oilseeds, 1.5% for Rabi, 5% for Annual Commercial/Horticultural crops.","Remaining premium subsidized equally by Central and State Governments.","Coverage for prevented sowing, localized calamities (hailstorm, cloudburst), and mid-season adversity."],f)
q=A.b(["Aadhaar Card","Land Record (Khatauni / Patta / Land Possession Certificate)","Sowing Certificate issued by Village Administrative Officer / Patwari","Bank Passbook copy showing IFSC"],f)
q=A.u3(A.b(["Step 1: Access the National Crop Insurance Portal (pmfby.gov.in) or enroll through bank / CSC.","Step 2: Submit crop insurance proposal before cut-off date for the respective season.","Step 3: Pay the subsidized farmer premium and collect insurance receipt/policy number.","Step 4: In case of crop loss, report within 72 hours via Crop Insurance Mobile App."],f),d,"Insurance","Provides affordable crop insurance coverage to stabilize farmers income against losses caused by droughts, floods, landslides, natural fire, pests, and unseasonal rains.",e,"scheme_pmfby",i,"Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY)","Department of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare","https://pmfby.gov.in",q,"Comprehensive crop insurance against non-preventable natural risks from pre-sowing to post-harvest.")
e=A.b(["All individual farmers, joint borrowers, tenant farmers, oral lessees, and sharecroppers.","Self Help Groups (SHGs) or Joint Liability Groups (JLGs) of farmers."],f)
d=A.b(["Credit limit up to \u20b93,00,000 at concessional interest rate of 7%.","Additional 3% prompt repayment incentive, reducing effective borrowing cost to just 4% per annum.","Collateral-free agricultural loans up to \u20b91,60,000.","ATM-enabled RuPay Kisan Card for easy withdrawals and input purchases."],f)
p=A.b(["Completed KCC Application Form","Identity & Address Proof (Aadhaar, Voter ID, PAN)","Land holding documents duly verified by revenue authority","Cropping pattern details for the upcoming season"],f)
p=A.u3(A.b(["Step 1: Obtain KCC form from local cooperative bank, commercial bank, or RRB.","Step 2: Fill personal and farm land holding details with proposed cropping plan.","Step 3: Submit to bank branch along with land documents.","Step 4: Bank issues sanctioned limit and RuPay card within 14 days."],f),d,"Credit & Loans","Simplifies credit delivery mechanism to meet short-term credit requirements for cultivation of crops, post-harvest expenses, farm asset maintenance, and allied activities like animal husbandry and fisheries.",e,"scheme_kcc","March 2025","Kisan Credit Card (KCC) Scheme","Reserve Bank of India & NABARD","https://www.nabard.org",p,"Concessional institutional credit at effective 4% interest rate for crop production and allied needs.")
e=A.b(["All categories of farmers with assured water source and agricultural land.","Small and Marginal farmers receive higher subsidy allocation (up to 55%)."],f)
d=A.b(["45% to 55% capital subsidy on Drip and Sprinkler irrigation equipment.","Saves 40-50% water while increasing crop yield by 20-30%.","Enables fertigation to deliver dissolved fertilizers directly to root zones."],f)
o=A.b(["Aadhaar Card","Land Record (RoR) & Electricity bill/water source proof","Passport size photograph","Bank account details"],f)
o=A.u3(A.b(["Step 1: Register through State Horticulture/Agriculture Department portal.","Step 2: Select registered micro-irrigation manufacturer/vendor.","Step 3: Field verification and GPS survey by horticulture officer.","Step 4: Installation followed by subsidy transfer to bank or vendor."],f),d,h,"Focuses on enhancing water use efficiency at farm level through precision micro-irrigation, moisture conservation, and farm ponds to achieve Har Khet Ko Pani and More Crop Per Drop.",e,"scheme_pmksy",i,"PM Krishi Sinchayee Yojana (Per Drop More Crop)","Ministry of Jal Shakti & Dept of Agriculture","https://pmksy.gov.in",o,"Up to 55% subsidy on micro-irrigation systems (Drip and Sprinkler) to maximize water use efficiency.")
e=A.b(["All farmers across India possessing agricultural land."],f)
d=A.b(["Detailed status report on 12 parameters: N, P, K, S, Zn, Fe, Cu, Mn, Bo, pH, EC, and OC.","Dosage advisory for specific crops to reduce wasteful fertilizer expenditure by 15-20%.","Guidance on soil amendments like gypsum or lime for alkaline/acidic soils."],f)
n=A.b(["Aadhaar Card","Land identification survey number","Mobile number for digital SMS delivery"],f)
n=A.u3(A.b(["Step 1: Soil samples collected by agricultural department field workers.","Step 2: Samples tested in designated district Soil Testing Laboratories (STLs).","Step 3: Soil Health Card generated and printed or downloaded via soilhealth.dac.gov.in."],f),d,g,"Assists farmers in improving productivity through judicious use of chemical fertilizers, organic compost, and micro-nutrients based on periodic laboratory soil analysis.",e,"scheme_soil_health","December 2024","Soil Health Card (SHC) Scheme","Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare","https://soilhealth.dac.gov.in",n,"Free soil testing and customized nutrient recommendations issued every 2 years.")
e=A.b(["Farmers organized into clusters of 20 or more members having 20 hectares land.","Willingness to transition away from synthetic inputs."],f)
d=A.b(["\u20b950,000 per hectare allocated for organic conversion, seeds, and bio-inputs.","\u20b931,000/ha transferred directly to farmer for procurement of bio-fertilizers and botanical sprays.","Free PGS-India organic certification."],f)
